# The towns in more depth: their trades, their worries, their neighbours, their stories. Larkfield, Ridgemere's salt
# pans and chapel, Frosthollow, Coldwater, Mirebridge, Southmeadow, Oakhaven, and the watch on the town walls.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Larkfield

scene ac_toll
when topic=smalltalk|work here.region=larkfield
a : The toll went up again at the gate. | Half the carters camp outside to dodge the toll. | Toll-keeper counted my wheels twice.
b[official] : The town sets the toll. I only take it.
b[carter] : Robbery with a ledger.
b : Of course it did. | Can't blame them. | You've got four. Always four.
a : Always. | No. | Ha.

scene ac_stables
when topic=work here.region=larkfield a.job=herder|carter|laborer
a : Forty beasts in the stable yard tonight. | A mule kicked me clean across the yard. | Hay's running low already.
b : Busy season. | Mules. Never trust a mule. | Order more.
a : Too busy. | Never again. | From where?

scene ac_inn_full
when topic=smalltalk here.region=larkfield here.place=tavern
a : Not a bed left at the Singing Lark. | Carters sleeping on the tables again. | Somebody's always singing at the Singing Lark.
b[innkeeper] : Full is good. Full is coin.
b : Every night. | On the tables! | Badly, too.
a : Every night. | Better than the mud. | Very badly.

scene wm_barrows
when topic=lore here.region=larkfield
a : Lights on the barrows again last night. | My grandfather dug into a barrow once. Never spoke of what he found. | Don't sleep on a barrow. You'll dream of the dead.
b[old] : Leave the barrows be. That's all anyone needs to know.
b[adolescent] : I'm going to camp on one. For a dare.
b : Shepherds' fires. | Wise of him. | I won't.
a : Maybe. | Very. | Don't.

scene wm_frontier_pride
when topic=smalltalk here.region=larkfield
a : Nobody tells us what to do out here. | City folk wouldn't last a winter on the downs. | Larkfield looks after its own.
b[old] : Our grandparents came out here to be free. Free, and hungry, some years.
b : Damn right. | Not a week. | Always has.
a : Damn right. | Not a day. | Always will.

scene wm_drovers
when topic=work here.region=larkfield a.job=herder|merchant|farmer
a : The drovers are in from the south with two hundred head. | Cattle prices fell when the drovers came in. | Wool's fetching a good price this year.
b : Busy market, then. | Always do. | Good. Sell, then.
a : Very. | Always. | I will.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ridgemere: the salt pans and the drowned

scene sr_pans
when topic=work here.region=ridgemere a.job=farmer|laborer
a : Raked the pans since dawn. | A dry wind, for once; the salt's coming fast. | Rain ruined a whole pan.
b : Hard work. | Good. | Bad luck.
a : Very. | For once. | Always is.

scene sr_drowned_bell
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
a : They ring the bell at the Chapel of the Tide for every boat lost. | The bell rang twice last winter. | My mother says she hears the drowned in the Sound.
b[priest] : We ring so they know we remember.
b : A sad sound. | Two boats? | Mine says the same.
a : Very. | Two. | Maybe they're right.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Frosthollow

scene ac_mountain_road
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Everyone going up to the mines stops here first. | The High Road's icy already on the climb. | Lowlanders always ask how far it is to the pits.
b[carter] : Far enough to kill a mule. I've seen it.
b : We're the doorstep of the mountain. | Take it slow. | Further than they think.
a : We are. | Slow and sure. | Always.

scene cb_cough
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Everyone in this town coughs. | Smoke's so thick today I can taste it. | My fur's grey with ore dust.
b[healer] : Breathe through a wet cloth when you're near the forge.
b[miner] : That's the taste of a living.
b : It's the forge. | Every day. | Everyone's is.
a : Always. | Always. | Everyone's.

scene cb_safe_return
when topic=lore here.region=frosthollow
a : Left a nail at the pithead shrine for my brother's safe return. | Hundreds of nails on the shrine wall now. | Every nail is somebody who came back up.
b[priest] : And every missing nail is somebody we pray for.
b : He'll come back. | So many. | A good custom.
a : He'd better. | So many. | It is.

scene cb_ser_ferro_road
when topic=smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
a : Ore carts go down the High Road to Ridgemere every day. | My daughter works in Ridgemere now. Never visits. | The city folk think we're savages up here.
b[old] : Half the iron in Ridgemere came down the High Road from here.
b : Every day, snow or sun. | Busy, probably. | Let them.
a : Every day. | Probably. | Let them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Coldwater

scene ls_boats
when topic=work here.region=coldwater a.job=fisher|crafter
a : New skiff's nearly done; just the pitch. | Somebody's been taking my boat at night. | Lake's too calm; the fish see the nets.
b : Fine-looking boat. | Chain it up. | Fish further out.
a : It'll float. | I will. | Further.

scene ls_mist
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.region=coldwater
a : Couldn't see the other end of the jetty this morning. | Mist comes in every dawn, lifts by noon. | The lake looks like milk.
b[old] : Glasswater breathes. That's the mist.
b : Every morning. | Like clockwork. | Pretty, though.
a : Every morning. | Always. | Very.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mirebridge

scene fh_cures
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=mirebridge
a : People come from all over for the marsh cures. | Bogmyrtle's tonic cured my cough. Or killed it. | Half the cures in the fens are poison, half are miracles.
b[healer] : The marsh is generous to those who know it.
b : The fens are famous for it. | Which half? | Pick carefully.
a : Famous. | Still coughing. | Very.

scene fh_floods
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.region=mirebridge
a : Water's up to the chapel stones again. | Boots never dry in this town. | The fen road's under water.
b[old] : It's always under water. That's the fens.
b : Raised for a reason. | Never. | Wade, then.
a : Always. | Never. | Ugh.

scene fh_peat
when topic=work here.region=mirebridge a.job=miner|laborer
a : Cut peat since dawn. | Found an old wooden thing deep in the peat. | Peat's wet; it won't sell.
b : Back-breaking. | What kind of thing? | Dry it.
a : Very. | Carved. Old. Strange. | In this weather?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Southmeadow

scene af_drought
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.region=southmeadow
a : Dust on everything. | No rain since the last moon. | Wells are getting low.
b[farmer] : If it doesn't rain soon, the second crop's lost.
b[old] : The sky takes its time. Rain will come.
b : Always dust in summer. | Pray for rain. | Share the water, then.
a : Always. | I am. | We must.

scene af_harvest
when topic=work here.region=southmeadow a.job=farmer|laborer|baker
a : Barn's full to the beams. | Good grain this year. Golden. | The miller's working night and day.
b : A good year. | Golden as butter. | Busy miller.
a : For once. | Gold, nearly. | Very busy.

scene af_ford
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=southmeadow
a : The orchards are spreading, they say. A row a year. | Toll at the gate pays for the watch. | My great-grandfather planted the first orchard here. Frost killed it.
b[old] : The land does what it likes.
b : Spreading? | Good use of it. | What happened?
a : Slowly. | Very. | A late frost.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Oakhaven

scene hm_carter
when topic=smalltalk here.region=oakhaven
a : The carter's a week late. | We're out of salt till the carter comes. | Do you think the carter's forgotten us?
b[old] : He always comes. Late, but he comes.
b : He'll come. | Borrow some. | Probably.
a : Eventually. | From whom? | Probably.

scene hm_valley
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=oakhaven
a : My family's lived in this wood for six generations. | The brook sings different before rain. | Nobody comes to Oakhaven by accident.
b[old] : And six more, I hope.
b : That's a long time. | Does it? | Nobody comes at all.
a : Long. | Listen. | Good.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The town walls

scene ft_watch_night
when topic=work here.region=towns a.job=guard here.time=night
a : Long night on the walls. | Something moved out past the ditch. | Stay awake. The sergeant checks.
b : They all are. | A fox. Probably. | Always.
a : Every night. | Probably. | Always.
